@SergeyKanzhelev  These test jobs are not using the `--image-config-file` parameter, Only the jobs for the test cases in the `e2e_node` tests will use this parameter.

I am not very familiar with this area and spent some time investigating the issue today:

They all use the `--gcp-node-image` parameter to define the node image (which includes the containerd version). This parameter ultimately takes effect in the k/k repo. If `--gcp-node-image` is GCI (the `--gcp-node-image` parameter is defined in kubetest and translates to the `NODE_OS_DISTRIBUTION` environment variable) and no other overriding variables are set, we will default to using the latest image from the [cos-121-lts](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/8dc51e11effa44e0698478ee23ebf18d72473b93/cluster/gce/config-default.sh#L91) image series to create nodes. Therefore, I think a more universal approach would be to update the default gci image version in the k/k repo (from `cos-121-lts` to `cos-125-lts`).

