@adityasharmawork: it looks like you posted the result of some AI tool. IMHO this added noise to the PR and worse, the conclusion is wrong. Next time, please consider whether some AI result is something that you fully understand and can explain - otherwise please don't post it. We only call that out for code submissions (https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/guide/pull-requests.md#ai-guidance, which may apply to some of your pending PRs?), but reviews are not different.

`TestListenerResyncPeriods` is a fairly complex test and sensitive to timing. @user12031, I tried to reproduce the failure as you described it, but I don't get to the goleak check because the `wg.Wait` is already stuck - same problem, though: a deadlock.

Here's a simpler reproducer:
```Go
func TestListenerStartup(t *testing.T) {
	// source simulates an apiserver object endpoint.
	source := newFakeControllerSource(t)
	source.Add(&v1.Pod{ObjectMeta: metav1.ObjectMeta{Name: "pod1"}})
	source.Add(&v1.Pod{ObjectMeta: metav1.ObjectMeta{Name: "pod2"}})

	// create the shared informer and resync every 1s
	informer := NewSharedInformer(source, &v1.Pod{}, 1*time.Second).(*sharedIndexInformer)

	// listener resync every 2s
	listener := newTestListener("listener", 2*time.Second, "pod1", "pod2")
	informer.AddEventHandlerWithResyncPeriod(listener, listener.resyncPeriod)

	stop := make(chan struct{})
	stopped := make(chan struct{})
	go func() {
		informer.Run(stop)
		close(stopped)
	}()

	// Let the resyncs start.
	time.Sleep(10 * time.Second)

	t.Log("stopping")
	close(stop)
	select {
	case <-time.After(10 * time.Second):
		t.Fatal("timed out waiting for informer to stop")
	case <-stopped:
		t.Log("stopped")
	}
}
```

It needs:
```patch
diff --git a/staging/src/k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go b/staging/src/k8s.io/client-go/tools/cache/shared_informer.go
