@dlipovetsky @pacoxu @HirazawaUi any additional comments from you?

@Goend: in your model, who creates the ResourceClaim? Scheduler or kube-scheduler?

With the current model, exactly one component is responsible for managing generated ResourceClaims (= kube-controller-manager). The different schedulers (could be more than one!) then react to ResourceClaims. That's a good separation of concerns, albeit with the effect that the scheduler needs to wait for the controller. I'm still not sure why you think that the added latency is a problem, or how much of a problem (quantitatively) it is.

Very recently, for support of extended resource API compatibility, we added creating a ResourceClaim in the scheduler binding phase. Now that we have figured out how to do that (there were some problems to be solved!), we could do the same for creation from template. But that's a significant change that would need a very strong justification.

https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/2a3a6605ac9b184711ef212ecbe26c8af4a8bac8/pkg/controller/resourceclaim/controller.go#L131-L214 
